<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 182-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 182-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 182-day</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills at Tuesday's auction and all of the</p>
<p>50 million litas issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, the</p>
<p>country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 10.84 percent, down from the 11.28</p>
<p>percent offered at the last auction for 182-day paper on April</p>
<p>8.</p>
<p>The settlement date is April 18 and the bills mature on</p>
<p>October 17.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>indicated.</p>
<p>SOLD  DAYS  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD  LAST AV. YIELD  DEMAND</p>
<p>50    182   10.50/11.10	10.84	   11.28	79.513</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
